DOCKER PRACTICAL – FULL STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION
STEP 1: Create Project Folder
mkdir docker-project
cd docker-project
STEP 2: Create HTML File
echo "Hello, World from Docker!" > index.html
STEP 3: Create Dockerfile
FROM nginx:latest
COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
STEP 4: Build Docker Image
docker build -t mywebimage .
STEP 5: Run Container with Port Mapping
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name mycontainer mywebimage
Access in browser:
http://localhost:8080
STEP 6: Stop Container
docker stop mycontainer
STEP 7: Remove Container
docker rm mycontainer
STEP 8: List Images
docker images
STEP 9: Alternative Lightweight Dockerfile (nginx:alpine)
FROM nginx:alpine
COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/
STEP 10: Common Docker Commands
docker ps # running containers
docker ps -a # all containers
docker logs
docker rmi
docker rm
docker build -t name .
docker run -d -p 8080:80 name
